In order to make recommendations to the board of commissioners of the county as to the formulation of current and long-range plans for transportation issues within the county, including, but not limited to, traffic congestion, road conditions, etc., the county transportation committee is hereby created and established. The county transportation committee shall be organized and empowered as set out in this division. The county transportation committee shall be created for the following purposes:
(1) To identify traffic problems in the county, e.g., safety, congestion, alternatives (multiuse paths), and other issues;
(2) To provide recommendations for short- and long-term priorities;
(3) To provide input, including recommendations and suggestions, on project alignments and alternatives;
(4) To assist with identification of funding sources, solicitation of federal funds, grants, etc.;
(5) To assist with coordination of projects between the county and the municipalities;
(6) To provide appropriate focus on projects to ensure accountability of staff and consultants:
(7) To provide recommendations for long-term goals (capacity, paths, senior services, etc.);
(8) To identify and support safety initiatives; and
(9) To assemble information and to facilitate communication of the county's views and concerns to GDOT and the Atlanta regional commission upon approval of the board of commissioners of the county.
It is the intent of the board of commissioners that the county transportation committee shall fully explore traffic issues and provide information and recommendations to the board of commissioners.
(Ord. No. 2016-03, § 2, 1-28-2016)

